# ReadCanvas — project rules

Source of truth for product: `docs/PRODUCT_BRIEF.md`. Follow that brief; do not add out-of-v1 features unless asked.

## Stack

- React + TypeScript + Vite. No backend in v1; static host only.
- Canvas of **letter objects** (e.g. Konva), not a single text field.
- PWA: cache the app and the letter model so the board works offline after first load.
- Persistence: last board only, in `localStorage` / IndexedDB. No login, no cloud sync.

## Recognition and speech

- On-device letter recognition only (TensorFlow.js or ONNX Runtime Web; A–Z / a–z). Never send strokes or images to a cloud OCR API.
- Convert a scribble after a short pause (multi-stroke letters), with an optional “I’m done.” Low confidence → a short picker, not a silent wrong letter.
- Keyboard insert skips recognition and places a letter on the board.
- TTS: Web Speech API (`speechSynthesis`). Language from the English / Indonesian toggle. Do not assume Indonesian voices exist on every device.

## Functional style

- Avoid classes and OOP (`class`, `extends`, `this` for domain logic). Prefer functions, plain data, and React function components + hooks.
- Model the board as data (arrays/records of letters) and pure functions that return new state. No mutable class stores.
- Side effects (canvas, IndexedDB, speech, model inference) live in small functions or hooks, not in class methods.
